  "query_preview": "..\nIssued at 158 PM CDT Tue Oct 6 2026\n\nTemperatures look more like late August/early September across the \nregion today. Breezy southwest winds have started to turn to the \nnorthwest behind a front which is draped across central Minnesota \nearly this afternoon. For the most part, Tds are still into the 50s \nahead of the front , but across southwestern Minnesota where \ntemperatures have made it into the mid 80s, we're seeing some RH \nvalues fall below 30%. Fire weather will be the main weather concern \nthrough this weekend given the warm and dry forecast. Tomorrow will \nbe a bit cooler than today, but it does look like RH values fall \ninto the 30s area wide. Did nudge down Tds a little, but they will \nlikely need to be adjusted further down which could bring those \nreadings into the near critical fire weather territory. \nAdditionally, northwest winds increase again by tomorrow afternoon \nwith gusts of around 25 MPH.  \n\nThursday will be the coolest day of the period, but still running a \nfew degrees above where we should be for early October. Moisture \nreturns Friday with southerly flow kicking in. There's a non-zero \nchance that far southern Minnesota may see some showers early Friday \nahead of a warm front that will continue to push north through \nthe weekend. Saturday's temperatures will likely be warmer than \ntoday with highs once again reaching into the mid 80s. This will\nbe another fire weather day to watch given this and winds \ngusting to 30 to 40 MPH. Thankfully, we'll have a bit more \nmoisture, but will need to monitor the potential for warmer \ntemperatures than what's currently in there. Another thing to \nconsider is what may happen with a tropical system in the Gulf \nduring this time period and what that would do to our moisture \nreturn. The forecast from Sunday onward becomes more uncertain \nwith the timing of a trough in the Pacific Northwest. PoPs and \nQPF have decreased a bit from 24 hours ago, but this still looks\nto be our best (and likely only) chance for precip during the \nforecast period. Temperatures will return to the 50s and 60s \nfollowing this system, but a few more warm days beyond this \nperiod are not out of the question.",
